        {
            "id": "257a79a5-b7aa-43fe-ae2e-4d86816728bc",
            "build_id": "a33b4c47-5286-4606-986f-dde3a0e1a0e6",
            "round_number": 5,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-07-10T00:43:32.843336+00:00",
            "notes": "For Round Five: I will take distortion - I just still love this combo with crep circle and  [Chain Evoker](item_812cc89e-feb0-47d0-9e03-9d8e33a80aca)! If you are really struggling for heals, you could pick  [Triage Unit](item_fec0554c-2685-4b93-822d-bf0020e654b4).\n\nWhen it gets later in the game like this it's more important to adjust items or powers as you need. I still take  [Distortion](item_5557e2f2-02df-4eac-8128-0c23b71183b1) most of the time - but it's good to have options.\n\nAt this point I would have previously taken  [Angelic Acrobatics](item_baad85fc-3da5-43af-ad9d-f17885f59aa5) - but I think it's just an option for certain matches. Sometimes, another weapon power or survival items will prove much more useful in the match.\n\nSo, at this point, the items you take really depend on the match - do you need healing or survival first?\n\n[Booster Jets](item_a291de85-b6d9-43cf-b5da-f3184a156f48) I like to take most matches for the chunk of weapon speed - the move speed can also help to survive. #\n\n[Caduceus Ex](item_9e7965ea-2abc-44a7-b042-950c6ad2fce7) is a new fav item - the increase in beam range will really help you keep a safer position esp in later rounds.  \n\n[Nebula Conduit](item_476b7040-54c9-4f0c-8283-b4407f6809f8) is very nice if you keep taking bursty damage which can become very high in these later rounds. Then  \n\n[Ogundimu Reduction Field](item_b12daf48-069b-44c1-88fe-221cbcff664d) field is a nice choice for sustained survival item.\n\nSo, in round give, I will start taking some of these items depending on what I need most and how much cash I have.  [Angelic Acrobatics](item_baad85fc-3da5-43af-ad9d-f17885f59aa5) is still an option too if you need the movement to survive.",
